// GPU settings preset: high-texture-4096, a control that fits no real device
//
// A texture edge of 4096 voxels and 32 GB of texture memory. No device is
// tested to render an edge above 2048. Some devices report a larger
// MAX_3D_TEXTURE_SIZE, but a reported size is not a reliable limit, so a
// deployment must not select this preset in production. Cornerstone3D marks
// the preset `internal`.
//
// The preset is the control of the demonstration. A series of up to 4096
// images renders with no reduction here, and the same series reduces under
// `gpu/medium`. The pair shows that the reduction comes from the limit and
// not from a defect. A real device can fail to allocate a texture of this
// edge, and that failure is the expected result on hardware.
//
// A preset applies only with final downsampling on, and a preset in this
// customization turns final downsampling on, also in a locked-down config.
// `?customization=` needs `customizationUrlPrefixes`, and config/default.js has
// none: there, set the preset through `customizationService` in the config.
// Nothing probes the device: a preset is a set of values, so a real device may
// hold more or less than the preset states.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/high-texture-4096`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuSettingsPreset": "high-texture-4096"
  }
}
